      row    7: ["`knowledge/gates-survey-kumitate.md`", "The six hermetic suites: executed case counts 62/42/60/102/39/43 (all `--selftest` exit 0; literal `check(` sites 62/42/60/71/35/41 \u2014 counts are loop-sensitive, so the executed summary line is the only honest count); uniform two-line close (`n/m` summary + `VERDICT:`, usage exit 64 everywhere); fail-closed arm inventories (proxy 12/12 arms fired, claims 5/5, kimi-census 1 token \u00d73 cases, round-gate 7 declared/6 fired with `INTERNAL_ERROR` uncovered, surface-probe + cite-check carry no token enum at all); verdict-line exactness tiers (full-line literal \u2192 anchored regex \u2192 startsWith \u2192 includes); mutation controls = cite-check's mutation copy (integration-gated, never under `--selftest`) + claims-check's external env-poison probe \u2014 no kill-rate harness or self-code fault injection anywhere in the corpus (I: the \"every declared kind fires\" meta-checks prove each branch is reached, not that a wrong implementation would be caught)", "kumitate-shokunin/scripts/*.mjs read-only; six `node <gate>.mjs --selftest` runs with exit codes + verbatim summary lines (note \u00a70); grep/wc censuses in-note"]
