Scope fact (reader premise): the stray-verdict scan and the verdict-table
keying run over the NOTE only. corpus/README.md is read by the reader only
for the `coverage` conjunct (last row naming the note), never for verdict
content. README pipe rows carrying KILLED/SURVIVED are therefore never
keyed — a scope boundary, not a declared limit of the plan.

