Reading: G1/G2 -> the reader's DELIM_RE (-{3,}) is STRICTER than S321's
'cells whose only content are hyphens': a GFM-legal one- or two-hyphen
delimiter is NOT a table to this reader, so its rows fall through to the
stray-verdict rule instead of the table rule.
G4 -> the reader RECOGNISES a table GFM says is not a table, and adds a
`delim:` finding (the plan's QUALITY 165 declares this rule).
G5 -> the reader's DELIM_RE accepts any leading whitespace, so a table
inside a 4-space INDENTED CODE block is keyed. S322 grounds only FENCED
blocks (4.5); S321 4.4 makes an indented block literal code too. This is
a class the plan's declared limits do not name.
G7 -> a blockquoted table is not keyed (the reader sees '>' in the cell).
G8/G9/G10/G11 -> the reader's remainder and break rules match S321.
G12/G13/G14/G15 -> norm_cell() lowercases and strips `*`/backticks, so the
header cell is matched case-insensitively (VERDICT, Verdict, `verdict`
all key) but only as the exact word `verdict` (`verdicts` does not).

