      row   10: ["`knowledge/gates-survey-kumitate.md` \u2014 round-2 addendum (K-R2-1\u20264, append-only)", "All six executed counts + artifact pins re-verified held on the current bytes (sha256 first16: cite-check `40573448\u2026`, surface-probe `148cbf85\u2026`, round-gate `f890e277\u2026`, proxy-check `a052ddb9\u2026`, claims-check `e9a21b44\u2026`, kimi-census `83016d45\u2026`; every `--selftest` exit 0 with verbatim summary lines \u2014 K-R2-1); \u00a77 meta-check anchor pair corrected to `claims-check.mjs:851-852` and `kimi-census.mjs:841-842` \u2014 the wave-1 ranges started early / ended short of both `check(...)` lines (K-R2-2); mutation-control census re-checked with the SKILL.md false hits excluded \u2014 still no gate ships a kill-rate harness (K-R2-3); cite-check integration group + round-gate `INTERNAL_ERROR` arm stay recorded-not-absorbed, sibling-owned (K-R2-4)", "kumitate-shokunin read-only; per gate `node scripts/<gate>.mjs --selftest` + `sha256sum scripts/<gate>.mjs`; `grep -n \"every finding kind fired by the suite\"` re-run 2026-10-14 (note \"Errata (round 2)\" block)"]
      row   11: ["`knowledge/gates-survey-kagi.md` \u2014 round-2 addendum (G-R2-1\u20266, append-only)", "\u00a71 claim-ledger pin corrected: **79301 B / sha256 first16 `93c5827202b9cdec`** \u2014 the surveyed 79294/`357fb245` was an intermediate dirty-tree state never committed; substrate moved 09:58:55, kagi's own round-18 `fecee87` (10:05:10) re-pinned `stamps.tsv` (G-R2-1); \u00a79 item 4's last-non-empty-line citation corrected `:53-56` \u2192 `:26-28` (G-R2-2); denied verbs 22 \u2192 **23** (G-R2-3); re-verified set held: six selftests 16/13/29/34/61/97 = 250, `--falsify` exit 1 `caught=16/18 failed=2` with the same two `SCOPE BREADTH-EXCEEDS` lines, F-1/F-2 standing and `corpus/README.md:43` still unqualified \"18/18\" (G-R2-4); \u00a78.1 [UNK] discharged \u2014 the mid-survey writer was kagi's own in-flight round-18 [INF] (G-R2-5); live verdicts 5/6 + F-2 fix stay sibling-owned recommendations (G-R2-6)", "kagi-shokunin read-only @ `fecee87`; `sha256sum`/`stat -c %s`, DENY_RE pipeline \u2192 23, `sed -n` line checks, spot selftests + `--falsify` re-run 2026-10-14"]
      row   12: ["`knowledge/verification-patterns-fleet.md` \u2014 round-2 addendum (TAMESHI-R2-4 extension + V-R2-1\u20264, append-only)", "Fourth pattern from game-dev-2d-shokunin's verifier machinery \u2014 D0\u2013D10: replays committed bytes (a commit lacking the change IS the finding, r64); mutants/faults are scratch-only runner fixtures; sensitivity = guard-disable in a disposable copy (binary per guard, no kill-rate tally \u2014 U8); a detected mutant must survive spoof classification and engine errors never count; opt-in probes proven inert unflagged; verifier writes its own instruments and recomputes from spec; 7-field regression fence vs prior receipts; falsification/failed verification kept first-class (r64 DISAGREE \u2192 landed bytes; r69 verifier-seat death recorded); receipts located (lessons-JSON era \u2192 in-tree scratch); declared bounds/non-writes \u2014 plus U8\u2013U13 and 2 predictions; explicitly single-lane, NOT general (PROVINCE.md); kaidoku census re-measured held (72 files; `verify:` 468 vs `verified-at:` 467, same four mismatched files), w6\u2013w8 AGREE tallies held (3\u00d75/5, 3\u00d75/5, 2\u00d76/6+1\u00d75/5), U1/U2 stay open with U1's first reading = grep-shape artifacts (V-R2-1\u20264)", "game-dev-2d-shokunin read-only @ `9fb50aa9` (LOG/SCORECARD/reports/corpus); census commands in-note \"Verification (extension)\"; kaidoku/wave re-greps re-run 2026-10-14"]
      row   13: ["`knowledge/mutation-case-kimi-census.md`", "Tameshi's first measured kill-rate (round 2, TAMESHI-R2-1): kumitate `kimi-census.mjs`'s 43-case hermetic suite against 10 single-edit mutants \u2014 one exact edit per fresh /tmp copy, driver asserts the old string unique, original byte-identical (sha256 before=after `83016d45\u2026`) \u2192 **8/10 killed (80 %)**, no inconclusive run, control 43/43 and every mutant still enumerating 43, 7.0 s sweep; survivors D2 (`findings.slice(0,6)`\u2192`(0,5)`: truncation boundary never exercised \u2014 max findings in any suite run = 2 vs cap 6, DRIFT asserts prefix-only) and D10 (`FROZEN.K2 25`\u2192`24`: only `frozen.K5` is asserted) \u2014 shared class \"reported-but-unasserted surfaces\"; per-kill failing-case labels (D4 = exactly the 3 root-enum cases, D8 = the 3 fail-closed cases, D1/D3 = 16 each incl. the exact green baseline); protected-arm inventory + measured gaps; errata E1 (author's D7-survivor expectation wrong \u2014 the fixtures' modes share floor bits); scope: measures the suite, not substrate drift [I]; U1\u2013U6", "kumitate-shokunin `scripts/kimi-census.mjs` @ `175de6ba` read-only (sha256 `83016d45\u2026`, 43273 B); mutants + per-defect evidence under `/tmp/tameshi-r2-1-work/` only; reproduce spec (10 edits + commands + D2/D10 sensitivity probes) in-note \u00a74"]
      row   14: ["`knowledge/mutation-case-kagi-census.md` \u2014 round 3 (TAMESHI-R3-1)", "Tameshi's second measured kill-rate, first bash gate: kagi `surface-census.sh`'s 16-case selftest vs 10 single-edit mutants \u2014 same method as round 2 (fresh `/tmp` copies, one exact edit each, count==1 gate, kagi tree never written; restore proof sha `275d8294\u2026` before=after, mtime 09:47:15, porcelain clean) \u2192 **8/10 killed (80 %)**, no inconclusive run, suite count held `(<n>/16 cases)` on every run, 11.0 s for 11 runs; survivors B5 (deleted exec x-bit arm: **fixture-absent arm** \u2014 no case reaches it, so no implementation moves the suite; non-equivalence probe: mutant reports `SURFACE OK \u2026 (exec 644)` where pristine reports `SURFACE DIVERGED` exit 1) and B10 (CLEAN-summary `ok=` arg swapped: reported-never-read count, same family as round-2 D10); kill is token-only in B4 (deleted symlink arm keeps exit=1, dies on the `SURFACE LINK` token assert); per-kill failing-case labels (B1 = case 05 undeclared-file, B3 = 3 incl. crosscheck-disagree, B8 = the two exit-2 setup cases); gate choice proven hermetic on this host (fixtures under `mktemp -d`; the 2 verbs cases `skip-case \u2026 substrate-absent` \u2014 `the-janitor` off PATH, kagi's own round-18 repair, LOG.md:741-744); E1: failing-case *counts* predicted 6/10 (case 04 is a second exit-0 green fixture, kills every green-firing defect); cross-language \u00a74: same headline as JS, narrower kill width (max 3/16 vs 16/43 \u2014 per-case fresh fixtures + exit+token asserts vs shared fixtures + exact-line asserts), shared survivor class reported-but-unasserted data, bash-only unreached-arm class; U1\u2013U6", "kagi-shokunin `corpus/surface-census.sh` @ `fecee87` read-only (sha256 `275d8294\u202653009f`, 44212 B, 886 newlines, 887th line unterminated); mutants + evidence under `/tmp/tameshi-r3-1-work/` only; reproduce spec (10 edits + commands + B5/B10 probes) in-note \u00a77"]
      row   15: ["`knowledge/executor-test-sufficiency.md` \u2014 round 3 (TAMESHI-R3-4)", "The no-oral-context executor test (SHONEN box 3 evidence): an executor with no tameshi context beyond `SKILL.md` @ `dd2f4dee\u20263753` reproduced **one killed mutant end-to-end** \u2014 D5, killed exactly as Appendix A records (`42/43 FAIL`, singleton failing case `MEMBER_MISSING \u2026 presence is gated`), control green 43/43 first try, all 10 manifest strings byte-exact and unique at their cited lines (`--check` \u2192 every `count=1`, `CHECK: all unique`), restore pin held; per-step sufficiency verdicts S1\u2013S10: 7\u00d7 SUFFICIENT, 2\u00d7 SUFFICIENT (latitude), 1\u00d7 ADDITIVE-IMPROVISATION (single-mutant `--only` subset is not described \u2014 affordance, not repair), 1\u00d7 NOT EXERCISED (survivor probe \u2014 D5 killed), 1\u00d7 ADAPTED (note format); the SKILL's grammar rule was load-bearing (a red mutant still prints `\u2026 42/43 pass`); contamination statement \u00a71 (read SKILL.md + target only, no corpus/plans/AGENTS); scope honest: ONE mutant of the JS case, not the full sweep [U3\u2013U6]; U6: no independent second lane had re-verified at write time \u2014 since closed by the round-3 audit replays (B2 re-ran D5 via the tool, same kill + same mutant sha)", "`tameshi-shokunin/SKILL.md` @ `dd2f4dee\u20263753` (45644 B, 665 lines) + kumitate `kimi-census.mjs` @ `175de6ba` (sha `83016d45\u2026` before=after); executor evidence under `/tmp/tameshi-r3-4-work/evidence/`; reproduce block in-note \u00a78"]
