==============================================================================
(c) presentation forms the reader does NOT key (declared limits)
==============================================================================
Declared limits of the plan (plans/round-94.plan.md, R94-C1 'Declared limits'):
  L1 a fenced block is literal text (S322): a fenced inverted table or a
     fenced `measured:` line is not keyed and does not refuse the note;
  L2 a table with no `verdict` cell in its header row is not a verdict table
     (S321): an id-keyed table that asserts no verdict is never refused;
  L3 a `verdict` cell outside the header row is a data cell (QUALITY 155);
  L4 a verdict word in prose with fewer than two pipes on the line is not a
     table row;
  L5 a cell containing an escaped `\|` is one cell (S321), so it does not
     shift the columns;
  L6 the counter certifies the twelve cells, not how they were obtained;
  L7 canary/unstable0 are declarations where C2 says so;
  L8 a fully-correct fence table plus a second fenced table that ALSO passes
     is not a refusal: the fence limit is a limit.

