  V5 -> data cell, not a header -> badrows=0, verdict_tables=1 (honest)
  V6 -> fenced -> badrows=0, verdict_tables=1 (honest, limit L1)
  V7 -> a 4-space INDENTED block is NOT a fence to this reader: keyed ->
        verdict_tables=2, badrows>0 (an UNDECLARED class: the plan's limit
        L1 names fenced blocks only; GFM/CommonMark also make a 4-space
        indented block literal code).
  V8 -> norm_cell() strips `*` and lowercases, so `**verdict**` IS a header
  V9/V10/V11 -> the DATA token is matched by EXACT string; a code span, a
        bold span or a lower-case spelling is NOT a verdict token
  V12 -> an escaped `\|` stays inside one cell (S321)

